From: aiueo52 <aiueo52@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 15:11:01 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 055/105] qwen4-exp moe: shared-expert gate early, join folded
 into HC apply (SGLANG_SHARED_GATE_EARLY)

`fused_gate_sigmoid_mul_add` runs after the routed/shared join, so its
1.7-2.1 us x 51 calls/step land on the critical path even though the gate
itself depends only on the MoE input.

Split it: `shared_expert_gate_sigmoid` computes the fp32 gate before the
dual-stream section -- on the current stream, which carries only the (short)
shared expert while the routed experts run on the alt stream -- and the MoE
hands `(shared_output, gate)` to the caller instead of doing the add. The
Qwen4Exp decoder layer passes them to the HC combine, whose apply stage forms
`bf16(routed + gate * shared)` and then the residual update in one kernel.

The gate stays fp32 and the routed+shared sum is rounded to bf16 before the
combine, exactly as the two-kernel order did, so the join is bit-identical;
the gate kernel reuses the fused kernel's block shape and warp count, so its
reduction tree -- and its value -- match as well.

Needs the gate at mix time to have an apply stage to fold into, so it implies
SGLANG_HC_GATE_EARLY=MOVED when R1 is left off. Default off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
